{
  "$comment": "Import spellings a consumer of @kingsleyweb/bun-ui writes, checked against the packed tarball by `bun scripts/consumer-check.ts packages/bun-ui` from the repo root. Every spelling here worked at some point; removing one hides a regression. An entry's `peers` names the optional peers it legitimately needs: it is checked in a consumer that has exactly them, and every entry without `peers` in one that has none, so the root and every `/<ui>/browser` entry are proved to need no domain package. `/jobs` needs bun-jobs (its types name `JobsApi`, and it throws bun-jobs' `ConfigError`); `/docs` and `/docs/hosted` need none. The `./docs/embed*` entries (the viewer's screens, for a host app that bundles them) are NOT here: TSX with CSS side-effect imports and React types, shipped as source, a bundler-only surface covered in-repo by the jobs app importing them by name (`app/jobs`), and by `__tests__/entryIsolation.test.ts`.",
